 3. **Constitution `TODO(PYTHON_VERSION)`** (R1) — pin to 3.11 before implementation begins.
 4. **Exit status for a closed stdout** (R7) — the spec is silent; implemented as 2 with a
    diagnostic, by analogy with SC-007.
+5. **Quadratic cost on an unbroken long token** (found during implementation, R2/R4) — the
+   email pattern's local part is deliberately unanchored (R4: "No boundary guard is placed on
+   the local part"), so inside an unbroken run of local-part characters
+   (`[A-Za-z0-9._%+-]`) every offset starts its own greedy attempt and the scan is O(n²) in
+   the run length. Measured on this environment: 10k characters 0.12 s, 25k 0.72 s, 50k
+   3.03 s, 100k **12.2 s**. Ordinary log lines are unaffected — the cost is per unbroken
+   run, and a 100,000-character line broken into word-sized tokens redacts in 0.01 s — but a
+   single 100,000-character token exceeds SC-008's whole-log 10 s budget on its own, and the
+   spec's "very long lines" edge case mandates exactly that size. Correctness is not
+   affected and is pinned by
+   `tests/test_fidelity.py::test_fr007_a_very_long_unbroken_run_is_still_correct`.
+
+   **The obvious fix is wrong.** Adding a left guard
+   (`(?<![A-Za-z0-9._%+-])`) to `EMAIL` makes the scan linear (100k in 0.009 s, 400k in
+   0.039 s) and looks behaviour-preserving, because leftmost-match semantics would never
+   start an email mid-run. It is not: after a *rejected* card candidate the scan loop
+   deliberately resumes at `start + 1` (R2), which can legitimately place `pos` inside a
+   local-part run, and the guard then blocks an email the unguarded pattern finds. A
+   differential fuzz of 200,000 random strings over an alphabet of
+   `[A-Za-z0-9@._%+\- ,:;/\t]` found 63 divergences, every one of them a **lost email** —
+   e.g. `6d_@edd` in `edf@2a4 \t--ca+fa@.5 6d_@edd@2`. Under-redaction is the failure mode
+   this feature exists to prevent, so the guard must not be applied.
+
+   Recommendation for the spec owner: either accept the cost and state a per-token bound in
+   the spec, or bound the work another way (for example cap the local part's length, which
+   changes the recognition contract and so needs an explicit decision). Implemented as
+   specified — the pattern is the normative contract verbatim.
